"""
gender_conversions.py
======================
Male<->female conversion tables for cosmetic ModMat slots (16-byte asset ID
+ material ID references, same "Array of byte" layout as every other
asset-data slot in the recipe). Kept in its own module, separate from
edit_skater_data.py, since these tables are pure lookup data generated
offline from the game's known mat vars rather than memory offsets.

Currently covers:
  - Head (the "Rostral" asset-data slot)
  - Eyes (the "Eyes" asset-data slot)

Both work the same way: read the current 16-byte value out of the slot,
look it up here, get back the opposite-gender value to write plus a
human-readable name.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Unequipped flag
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Both the asset ID half and the material half of an asset-data slot use this
same 8 bytes repeated when nothing is equipped there (same sentinel used
for the Missing Texture "already unequipped" safety check elsewhere in the
tool). Any conversion function here returns None immediately if the current
value is this flag - there's nothing to convert if nothing's equipped.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Head Gender
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Every male head has facial hair baked into its name/material (stubble,
beard, soulpatch, magnum, billygoat, goatee, handlebar, or none) plus an
eyebrow style/color and sometimes a separate haircap color; female heads
only vary by skin tone, hair color, and eyebrow style/number (no facial
hair option at all). So there's no lossless 1:1 conversion - this table is
a best-effort match built by:
  - dropping facial hair entirely when converting male -> female (there's
    nowhere for it to go)
  - carrying hair color over from the male head's haircap color when it
    has one, otherwise from its facial hair color, otherwise a fallback
  - matching eyebrow style directly (male styles 1-4 <-> female
    eyebrow01-04); female eyebrow05/06 have no male equivalent so those
    get approximated by reusing the style 1/2 pattern
  - going female -> male always lands on a bald (no facial hair) male head
    with the matching skin tone, eyebrow style/color, and hair color set
    via haircap - since female -> male is a many-to-one problem otherwise

HEAD_GENDER_SWAP covers every stock head in both directions - all 470 male
heads and all 36 female heads.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Eye Gender
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Eyes are simpler: same 5 color names (lightbrown, darkbrown, darkblue,
lightblue, green) exist for both genders, just under different mod IDs, so
EYE_GENDER_SWAP is an exact, lossless 1:1 swap in both directions - no
approximation needed.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Both HEAD_GENDER_SWAP and EYE_GENDER_SWAP are keyed by the *current*
16-byte ModMat as an uppercase hex string. Each value is
(target_modmat_hex, target_name). A current value that isn't a key (and
isn't the unequipped flag) simply isn't a recognized stock item for that
slot - callers should treat a miss as "not recognized" rather than an
error.
"""

UNEQUIPPED_FLAG = bytes.fromhex("01678C486213905901678C4862139059")


def is_unequipped(current_16_bytes: bytes) -> bool:
    return current_16_bytes == UNEQUIPPED_FLAG


